course: dictionary
lesson: 6567
title: Family words: niece
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A niece is the daughter of your brother or sister. If your mum has a brother, his daughter is your niece. Look for the clues in the sentence: «my niece», «nieces and nephews» and «great-niece» all tell you the word is about family.
explain: Family words come in pairs. An aunt or uncle is the sister or brother of your mum or dad, and a niece or nephew is the child of your brother or sister. A niece is one generation below you on a sideways branch of the family tree, so check which branch she is on before you decide.
explain: Some words sound alike but mean different things. «nis» is a Ukrainian word that means nose, and it sounds just like the English word niece. Sound is only a clue, so always check the meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: A niece is the daughter of your brother or sister, or of your husband's or wife's brother or sister.
fact: «My niece» means the daughter of my brother or sister.
fact: A boy in the same family position is a nephew.
fact: «Nieces and nephews» means the children of your brothers and sisters.
fact: «nis» (Ukrainian) means nose, and it sounds like English «niece».
exercise: «My niece is coming to stay this weekend.» Who is my niece? | *The daughter of my brother or sister | A boy who is my brother's son | My friend from school | My mum's mum
exercise: «The eye is Oko, and the nose is nis, which sounds just like English niece.» What does nis mean? | Eye | *Nose | Ear | Ukrainian word for niece
exercise: «Nieces and nephews» are the children of your brothers and sisters. Which word is the boy version of niece? | Aunt | Uncle | *Nephew | Nose
test: If your brother has a daughter, what is she to you? | A sister | A nose | *A niece | An aunt
test: The Ukrainian word «nis» sounds like niece. What does it mean? | Eye | *Nose | Ear | Neck
exam: Your mum's brother has a daughter. What is she to you? | Your niece | Your aunt | Your sister | *Your cousin
